The production code is internal and sealed, and the refactor tool is not available to make methods virtual for testing. Also, the StoreWrapper class is sealed, so I cannot subclass it to inject test behavior. Given these constraints, I will write a test that uses Moq to create a mock ILogger and a partial mock of MultiDatabaseManager using reflection or dynamic proxy is not possible here. Instead, I will test the RecoverCheckpoint method by invoking it and verifying that the ILogger.LogInformation extension method is called by setting up the environment to cause the exception and log call. I will submit a test that mocks ILogger and calls RecoverCheckpoint, verifying the log call indirectly by capturing the ILogger calls. I will submit the test now. 

